  message: "RE-CHECK 2026-11-02 on dev ae02786fca (WI-jomik acceptance sweep, after PR #2004: shared resolvers no longer guess among tied candidates; PR #2006: a Rust method call never binds a free function). VERDICT: PARTLY. Repro run: /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_member_recheck_11022026/scratch_C/niriz/lila and /spark (copies of p3_review langs2 fx_niriz/fx_niriz2, plus Use2: import TypeCheckResult; TypeCheckResult.DataTypeMismatch(\"y\").describe()); hypergumbo survey; pytest test_scala_return_type_registry.py::TestSameNamedTypesInTwoPackages. Observed: FIXED (object): U.f -> core/Granter.scala:4-4:Granter.check, V.g -> sec/Granter.scala:4-4:Granter.check. STILL: Use.a Literal(1).eval() -> scala:sp.catalyst.expressions.Literal:0-0:eval:external_symbol 0.4; Use.c l.eval() same; Use.b/Use.d describe -> ...TypeCheckResult.DataTypeMismatch:0-0:describe:external_symbol; Use2.e -> scala:external:0-0:describe; Ctl.chal -> scala:lila.challenge.Env:0-0:version:external_symbol (only tour resolves); TestSameNamedTypesInTwoPackages 1 passed (still asserts resolved == 1). Note: Matches the 2026-11-01 PARTLY-STALE description. Object members work; case class, typed parameter, nested-type and class-typed receivers stay external. The sbt inherited-through-object withhold was not built. Fixtures: /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/jomik_member_recheck_11022026/scratch_*/."  # e71a
